§3.2 contextual emission — insertion into a specifier sequence (from the tsx
soak: useCallback added to React named imports; sibling specifiers vary per
file). Needs sequence-delta emission: scope = the import clause, delta = the
inserted specifier, remaining specifiers as a sequence metavar. The WidgetView
site inserts at alphabetical mid-position with a prettier multi-line reflow —
its t'' would differ from the after in specifier order, so it stays an honest
residual.

The v1 insertion channel (ellipsis-context, edge positions) does not cover
this case even though UserList/UserPanel insert at the prepend edge: the
imports are ONE-LINE, so the emitted rule's [+] splice is inline and cannot
reproduce the site's spacing byte-exactly (` useCallback, ` needs the
surrounding one-line spacing convention, i.e. separator/spacing synthesis).
Line-structured containers are covered by ts_decorator_flag_insert /
kotlin_arg_prepend_insert; this fixture is the inline + mid-position tier.
